From: Automation Platform controller <controller@pipefail.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 0003] prefetch execution_environment on the unified jobs list

Implements: D-4 (CTL-052) — measured with the profiling in
reports/ctl-050-first-probe.md follow-up: the jobs list view ran 33 SQL
queries per 20-row page, 20 of them identical per-row execution_environment
lookups from summary_fields. Adding execution_environment to JobAccess.select_related (the class behind
/api/v2/jobs/) and UnifiedJobAccess.prefetch_related removes the last N+1 on
the hottest list endpoints. (The 424ms "idle list latency" previously attributed
to serialization turned out to be Basic-auth PBKDF2 per request — by design;
the console's trusted-header path does not pay it.)

Tested by: build/test.sh baseline (no test-count change expected) and the
before/after query-count measurement on prod1.

diff --git a/awx/main/access.py b/awx/main/access.py
index e3410b2..9534af8 100644
--- a/awx/main/access.py
+++ b/awx/main/access.py
@@ -1660,6 +1660,9 @@ class JobAccess(BaseAccess):
         'inventory',
         'project',
         'project_update',
+        # summary_fields serializes the EE per row; without this it is the one
+        # remaining N+1 on the jobs list (20 extra queries per page).
+        'execution_environment',
     )
     prefetch_related = (
         'organization',
@@ -2489,6 +2492,7 @@ class UnifiedJobAccess(BaseAccess):
         'unified_job_template',
         'instance_group',
         'credentials__credential_type',
+        'execution_environment',
         Prefetch('labels', queryset=Label.objects.all().order_by('name')),
     )
 
